=== file: README.md ===
# FAQ customer support workflow

This workflow drafts an answer using the product FAQ, classifies whether the cited evidence clearly supports it, and sends unsupported or uncertain questions to a human for follow-up. Customer content is treated as potentially personal; the FAQ answerer masks PII and the handoff contains only the question and relevant context.

## Configuration

Set `PRODUCT_FAQ_ROOT` to the directory containing the organization-provided FAQ. Set `SUPPORT_API_URL` to the approved support API base URL before configuring the HTTP tools.

The HTTP tools are declared with restricted paths, but are deliberately not granted to the FAQ answerer. The plan provides only one agent, and that agent reads customer-supplied text and the FAQ; giving it tools that send messages or create tickets would combine untrusted input, private-data access, and external effects. Consequently, this project does not send the grounded answer, create a ticket, or send a handoff confirmation. It asks HandoffApprover and CustomerSupport to handle the handoff manually, and it explicitly reports that the actions were not performed. To enable those integrations safely, add a separate effect-only agent that receives only typed, minimized values and requires approval for ticket creation and handoff confirmation.

Run the workflow tests with `weave test main.loom`.
=== end===
